        "Development should expand the circle of concern while retaining the legitimate responsibilities that support it.",
        "7.4 Apply the pattern to decisions\nWhen evaluating a proposed change, ask:\n1. What limitation is the new approach trying to overcome?\n2. What useful function does the old approach perform?\n3. Which parts must be preserved?\n4. What new capability does the change create?\n5. What dependencies could be damaged if the old system is discarded?\n6. What new risks appear at the next level of complexity?\nThis is useful when evaluating technology, organisational change, education, business models, and personal development."
